# 3. Errors.
CALL java_stats_more_errors(@e);
SELECT @e AS errors;
errors
the window must be at least 1 row, not 0
minPeriods must be from 1 to the window (2), not 3
unknown statistic 'mode' (mean, sum, var, std, min, max, median, quantile:q, mad)
'quantile:high': the quantile must be a number, as quantile:0.9
a quantile must be in [0, 1], not 2.0
mu must be a finite number, not NaN
column 'sensor' is not a DATE, DATETIME or TIMESTAMP (CAST(... AS DATETIME) in the query makes it one)
'5': a width is a number and a unit, as '5 MINUTE' or '1 DAY'
'five MINUTE': the number must be a whole number, as '15 MINUTE'
'0 MINUTE': the width must be at least 1
'5 FORTNIGHT': unknown unit 'FORTNIGHT' (MICROSECOND, MILLISECOND, SECOND, MINUTE, HOUR, DAY, WEEK, MONTH, QUARTER, YEAR)
'yesterday' is not a date or time as MySQL writes it ('2026-11-27' or '2026-11-27 10:05:00')
the width must be a positive number, not 0.0
unknown method 'spline' (null, locf or linear)
two rows at 2026-11-27 10:00:00: aggregate first (bucket, then groupBy)
the partition column cannot be the time column
more than 1000000 steps of 1 MICROSECOND to fill: a larger step, or a shorter range
the frame has 9 rows, the column 2
the column needs a name
'2026-13-01' is not a date or time as MySQL writes it ('2026-11-27' or '2026-11-27 10:05:00')
more than 1000000 steps of 1 SECOND from 2026-01-01 to 2126-01-01: a larger step, or a shorter range
DROP TABLE readings, days, ticks;
DROP FUNCTION stats_more_selfcheck;
DROP PROCEDURE java_series;
DROP PROCEDURE js_series;
DROP PROCEDURE py_series;
DROP PROCEDURE java_stats_more_errors;
REVOKE CREATE_JAVA_ROUTINE, CREATE_JAVASCRIPT_ROUTINE, CREATE_PYTHON_ROUTINE ON *.* FROM root@localhost;
UNINSTALL COMPONENT "file://component_mle";
